module gunbc.scm.supersession

// THE DESTINATION, MADE TO REQUIRE THE PROOF IT ACTS ON.
//
// Superseding a head slot destroys a generation. Until this module the operation was authorized by
// `standing_may_supersede_generation : LoadStanding -> Bool`, and a Bool carries none of what the
// decision depends on: not the exact generation the evidence was gathered from, not the document
// identity actually examined, not the schema identity under which malformedness was established,
// and no receipt joining the refusal to this policy arm. Every route into that predicate was
// therefore equally authoritative, including a route that manufactured a wrong cause -- which is
// the class `test.claim.coproduct_payload_soundness_witness` closes ONE producer of, while
// recording that closing producers does not bound the population of routes.
//
// SO THE FIX IS AT THE DESTINATION AND IT IS A SHAPE CHANGE, NOT A CHECK. Three things move:
//
//   1. EVIDENCE IS MINTED FROM THE SLOT, NEVER SUPPLIED ALONGSIDE IT. `observe_generation` takes the
//      live `HeadSlot` and derives `observed_generation` from it. A caller cannot state which
//      generation it examined; it can only examine one. `SupersessionEvidence` is `sole_constructor`
//      and its mint is `admit_callers`-sealed to that one observer, so there is no second route to
//      an evidence value and no record literal anywhere else can forge one.
//
//   2. ACTUATION IS COMPARE-AND-SWAP AGAINST THAT SAME GENERATION. `supersede_head_slot` refuses
//      unless the slot still holds the generation the evidence was gathered from. A slot that moved
//      between the read and the write is `GenerationMovedUnderEvidence` -- a typed, located refusal
//      naming both generations, never a widen and never a retry (DESIGN section 5).
//
//   3. THERE IS NO STANDALONE PERMISSION VALUE TO CARRY AROUND. Authorization and swap are one
//      operation returning the new slot together with its warrant, so a warrant is a RECEIPT of a
//      swap that happened rather than a capability that could be replayed against a later
//      generation. A permission that can outlive the observation it rests on is the same defect one
//      level out, and a separate `authorize` returning a reusable token would have re-introduced it.
//
// WHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM. It does not establish that any producer of `LoadDocumentMalformed` is
// correct; it establishes that a wrong one no longer suffices, because a cause alone no longer
// authorizes anything. The audit of the relation's producer side is
// recorded on `standing_permission_refusal` below.
//
// dissolve-on: none.

import std.types { Bool, String }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }
import gunbc.scm.object_store { ObjectId, object_id_eq }
import gunbc.scm.load_standing {
  LoadStanding, LoadComplete, LoadPartial, LoadUnsupportedProtocol,
  LoadDocumentMalformed, LoadIdentityCollision,
}

// A NAMED PLACE HOLDING EXACTLY ONE GENERATION. The slot is the unit supersession destroys, so it
// is the unit the compare-and-swap is denominated in. `generation` is a content address rather than
// a counter deliberately: a counter says a generation is newer, an address says WHICH generation,
// and the CAS below needs the second.
type HeadSlot {
  slot: String
  generation: ObjectId
}

// THE FOUR FACTS THE BOOL COULD NOT CARRY, in one value that cannot be assembled without an
// observation. `observed_generation` is derived from the slot by the observer; `examined_root` is
// what the reader actually read, and the two are JOINED in the refusal relation rather than assumed
// equal -- evidence gathered from a document other than the one the slot holds is exactly the
// failure this field exists to name. `schema_identity` is the tag whose match is what makes
// malformedness a claim about a document rather than about this reader's limits.
type SupersessionEvidence sole_constructor {
  slot: String
  observed_generation: ObjectId
  examined_root: ObjectId
  schema_identity: String
  standing: LoadStanding
  authority: DeclarationRef
}

// THE RECEIPT OF A SWAP THAT HAPPENED. It names both generations, so a reader of the receipt can ask
// what was destroyed and what replaced it without consulting the slot, which by then has moved on.
type SupersessionWarrant sole_constructor {
  slot: String
  superseded_generation: ObjectId
  installed_generation: ObjectId
  schema_identity: String
  authority: DeclarationRef
}

// FIVE REFUSALS FOR FIVE REASONS, each naming the quantities it compared. `StandingDoesNotPermit`
// carries the standing rather than collapsing to a bare refusal: the caller that offered
// `LoadUnsupportedProtocol` and the caller that offered `LoadPartial` made different mistakes with
// different remedies (fetch a newer reader / supply the missing objects), and a shared arm would be
// the state-space conflation DESIGN names.
type SupersessionRefusalCause
  = StandingDoesNotPermit { standing: LoadStanding }
  | EvidenceNamesAnotherSlot { evidence_slot: String, actuation_slot: String }
  | EvidenceExaminedAnotherDocument { observed: ObjectId, examined: ObjectId }
  | GenerationMovedUnderEvidence { observed: ObjectId, current: ObjectId }
  | ProposedGenerationIsTheObserved { generation: ObjectId }

type SupersessionOutcome
  = SupersessionApplied { slot: HeadSlot, warrant: SupersessionWarrant }
  | SupersessionRefused { cause: SupersessionRefusalCause }

fn mint_supersession_evidence(
  slot: String,
  observed_generation: ObjectId,
  examined_root: ObjectId,
  schema_identity: String,
  standing: LoadStanding,
  authority: DeclarationRef,
) -> SupersessionEvidence
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.scm.supersession", decl_name: "observe_generation"),
  ]
  = SupersessionEvidence {
    slot: slot,
    observed_generation: observed_generation,
    examined_root: examined_root,
    schema_identity: schema_identity,
    standing: standing,
    authority: authority,
  }

// THE ONLY ROUTE TO EVIDENCE, AND IT TAKES THE SLOT. Nothing here judges the standing -- classifying
// a format's refusals is that format's own job (gunbc.scm.load_standing states why) -- but the
// generation the evidence is BOUND to is not the caller's to state. That is the difference between
// a value that describes an observation and a value that IS one.
fn observe_generation(
  slot: HeadSlot,
  examined_root: ObjectId,
  schema_identity: String,
  standing: LoadStanding,
  authority: DeclarationRef,
) -> SupersessionEvidence {
  mint_supersession_evidence(
    slot: slot.slot,
    observed_generation: slot.generation,
    examined_root: examined_root,
    schema_identity: schema_identity,
    standing: standing,
    authority: authority,
  )
}

// THE AUDIT OF THE AUTHORIZATION RELATION, at the denominator the hazard actually has: this
// destination's whole producer side, not any one defect site. Measured on the live tree rather than
// recalled, by enumerating every declaration that returns a `LoadStanding`.
//
//   PRODUCERS, TOTAL: two, both in `gunbc.scm.commit_closure_json_v2`.
//     `closure_document_load_standing` classifies one format's refusals. It descends everywhere a
//       payload could hide a second distinction -- through `MemberReadRefusal`'s four modes and
//       `TargetReferenceRefusal`'s four -- and is the ONLY declaration in the tree that can return
//       `LoadDocumentMalformed`, so it is the entire permitting surface.
//     `loaded_closure_standing` answers only `LoadComplete` or `LoadPartial`. The success path is
//       therefore OUTSIDE this relation by construction, not by a check: no load that succeeded can
//       authorize destroying what it read.
//     `closure_document_standing` is the join of the two and mints no standing of its own.
//
//   CONSUMERS BEFORE THIS MODULE: none in production. The permitting predicate had witnesses and no
//     caller, so the hazard was not live -- it was pre-positioned, waiting for the first actuator to
//     be written against the shape that was there. That is why the repair is a shape change landing
//     WITH the actuator rather than a guard added to one.
//
//   A NEIGHBOUR THAT IS NOT A ROUTE, checked rather than assumed. `gunbc.scm.repository_envelope`
//     decodes the envelope that names a head and carries its own `RepositoryDecodeRefusal`, and it
//     classifies NOTHING into `LoadStanding`. DESIGN's recurring-failure-mode census records
//     `repository_load_disposition` collapsing thirteen `ImageRefusal` arms as a specimen of the
//     total-but-blind class; that symbol no longer exists in the tree, and the envelope decoder has
//     no route to this destination today. The specimen stands as a historical record; it is not a
//     second live producer, and reporting it as one would have inflated the population from one
//     measurement and one recollection.
//
//   WHAT THE AUDIT DOES NOT ESTABLISH. One producer today is not a bound on producers tomorrow, and
//     that is precisely why the destination now demands evidence instead of trusting a cause: a new
//     classifier reaches `supersede_head_slot` on the same terms as the old one, and neither can
//     supply a generation it did not read.
//
// THE PERMISSION ARM, DESCENDING RATHER THAN ANSWERING true/false. This is the same relation the
// deleted Bool encoded, and the difference is that a refusal now names which standing refused it, so
// a sixth standing fails to compile HERE rather than inheriting whichever answer a wildcard gave it.
fn standing_permission_refusal(standing: LoadStanding) -> SupersessionRefusalCause? {
  match standing {
    LoadDocumentMalformed => none
    LoadComplete => Present { value: StandingDoesNotPermit { standing: LoadComplete } }
    LoadPartial => Present { value: StandingDoesNotPermit { standing: LoadPartial } }
    LoadUnsupportedProtocol =>
      Present { value: StandingDoesNotPermit { standing: LoadUnsupportedProtocol } }
    LoadIdentityCollision =>
      Present { value: StandingDoesNotPermit { standing: LoadIdentityCollision } }
  }
}

// THE ORDER IS PART OF THE CONTRACT. Slot identity first, because evidence about another slot is not
// weak evidence about this one; then the standing, which is the policy question; then the join
// between what was observed and what was examined; then the compare-and-swap; then the degenerate
// proposal. Reporting the first cause rather than all of them is deliberate here and not a
// counted-diagnostics violation: these are not independent findings about one document, they are
// preconditions in a chain where a later comparison is meaningless once an earlier one has failed.
fn supersession_refusal(
  slot: HeadSlot,
  evidence: SupersessionEvidence,
  proposed_generation: ObjectId,
) -> SupersessionRefusalCause? {
  if evidence.slot != slot.slot {
    Present {
      value: EvidenceNamesAnotherSlot {
        evidence_slot: evidence.slot,
        actuation_slot: slot.slot,
      },
    }
  } else {
    match standing_permission_refusal(standing: evidence.standing) {
      Present { value: cause } => Present { value: cause }
      Absent =>
        if !object_id_eq(left: evidence.examined_root, right: evidence.observed_generation) {
          Present {
            value: EvidenceExaminedAnotherDocument {
              observed: evidence.observed_generation,
              examined: evidence.examined_root,
            },
          }
        } else if !object_id_eq(left: evidence.observed_generation, right: slot.generation) {
          Present {
            value: GenerationMovedUnderEvidence {
              observed: evidence.observed_generation,
              current: slot.generation,
            },
          }
        } else if object_id_eq(left: proposed_generation, right: slot.generation) {
          Present { value: ProposedGenerationIsTheObserved { generation: proposed_generation } }
        } else {
          none
        }
    }
  }
}

fn mint_supersession_warrant(
  slot: String,
  superseded_generation: ObjectId,
  installed_generation: ObjectId,
  schema_identity: String,
  authority: DeclarationRef,
) -> SupersessionWarrant
  admit_callers: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.scm.supersession", decl_name: "supersede_head_slot"),
  ]
  = SupersessionWarrant {
    slot: slot,
    superseded_generation: superseded_generation,
    installed_generation: installed_generation,
    schema_identity: schema_identity,
    authority: authority,
  }

// AUTHORIZATION AND SWAP ARE ONE OPERATION. There is no window between them because there is no
// intermediate value: the warrant is minted from the same comparison that produced the new slot, and
// it cannot be minted anywhere else. A caller holding a warrant holds a record of a generation that
// is already gone, which is the only thing it is safe for a warrant to be.
fn supersede_head_slot(
  slot: HeadSlot,
  evidence: SupersessionEvidence,
  proposed_generation: ObjectId,
) -> SupersessionOutcome {
  match supersession_refusal(
    slot: slot,
    evidence: evidence,
    proposed_generation: proposed_generation,
  ) {
    Present { value: cause } => SupersessionRefused { cause: cause }
    Absent =>
      SupersessionApplied {
        slot: HeadSlot { slot: slot.slot, generation: proposed_generation },
        warrant: mint_supersession_warrant(
          slot: slot.slot,
          superseded_generation: slot.generation,
          installed_generation: proposed_generation,
          schema_identity: evidence.schema_identity,
          authority: evidence.authority,
        ),
      }
  }
}

// RUNG HONESTY (DESIGN section 4b), declared rather than left to be rediscovered, and MEASURED
// rather than read off the type declarations.
//
// WHAT IS CLOSED. `SupersessionEvidence` cannot be forged and `mint_supersession_evidence` cannot be
// reached except through `observe_generation`, so no caller can state a generation it did not read.
// Both probes ran against this module from `test.claim.scm_supersession_witness` (bold-crane-188,
// 2026-08-26, base 151e771461) and both refused at resolve:
//   a cross-module record literal returned "sole_constructor type 'SupersessionEvidence' cannot be
//     constructed outside its defining module";
//   a direct call to the mint returned "constructor call admission refused:
//     'gunbc.scm.supersession.mint_supersession_evidence' refuses call from
//     'test.claim.scm_supersession_witness.probe_direct_mint' -- permitted callers:
//     [gunbc.scm.supersession.observe_generation]".
// A control on the unmodified file compiled and executed green in the same dispatch, so the refusals
// are load-bearing rather than a harness that refuses everything. Both probes were removed after
// measurement, because neither has a RED that survives inside an accepted module -- what keeps them
// honest in the enrolled suite is that every applied supersession there routes through
// `observe_generation`. `SupersessionWarrant` is sealed the same way to `supersede_head_slot` and was
// not separately probed; it is the same mechanism at the same rung, and saying so is weaker evidence
// than the two measurements above, which is why it is said here rather than counted with them.
//
// WHAT IS NOT CLOSED, and it is the honest ceiling rather than an oversight. The walls confine WHO
// may construct evidence, not WHETHER the standing inside it is true: `observe_generation` accepts
// whatever standing its caller classified, so a producer that mis-classifies a document still
// reaches `LoadDocumentMalformed` here. That is unchanged by design -- classifying a format's own
// refusals belongs to that format (gunbc.scm.load_standing) -- and what changed is that a correct
// standing is no longer SUFFICIENT: the swap additionally requires the slot to still hold the
// generation the classification was made against. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a second head-slot format, at
// which point the classifier obligation is derivable from two members rather than guessed from one.
fn supersession_applied(outcome: SupersessionOutcome) -> Bool {
  match outcome {
    SupersessionApplied { slot: _, warrant: _ } => true
    SupersessionRefused { cause: _ } => false
  }
}
